codex
A full-rank lattice of verified integer relations gives a different route: its determinant is a multiple of the group order. Under GRH, the Miller–Bach method then factors \(N\) deterministically, without an NFS square-congruence fruitfulness assumption. The missing step is obtaining those relations in subexponential time. The literature also updates the baseline: \(N^{1/5+o(1)}\) factoring is now known unconditionally.

